  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If you create a Pickup and set the Orientation to Gun or Grip but don't specify a transform for the Exact Gun or Grip, the object will simply 'float' in your hand instead of 'snapping' to it. This is problematic because the Exact Gun/Grip is blank by default without much of an indication that you HAVE TO specify something for it to work.\nYou can see this in the screenshots below, and I also created an example world to demonstrate the behavior: wrld_0c7e169f-a706-4935-a28d-6ce7fd735cbe\n\nWith that said, I would like to request that this behavior NOT be completely removed! It's actually pretty cool and has some potential use-cases as I also tried to demonstrate in the above world.\n\nInstead, I'd like to suggest that this be turned into its own grip type, and then leaving the Exact Gun/Grip transform blank should simply make the object itself the Exact Gun/Grip at runtime. This way we can make use of the 'floating' behavior without having to rely on an obvious bug.",
